{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"options":{"content":"","images":{},"widgets":{}},"periodicTable":false,"type":"multiple"},"hints":[{"content":"###Background \n\nThe imaginary unit $\\maroonD{i}$ is defined as $\\sqrt{-1}$. So for any negative real number $-a$, we can express $\\sqrt{-a}$ as $\\maroonD{i}\\sqrt{a}$. ","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"###Converting the Expression \n\n\u003e$\\begin{align}\\pm\\sqrt{-80}\u0026=\\pm\\sqrt{-1\\cdot80}\n\\\\\\\\\u0026=\\pm\\sqrt{-1}\\cdot\\sqrt{80}\n\\\\\\\\\u0026=\\pm\\maroonD{i}\\cdot\\sqrt{80}\n\\\\\\\\\u0026=\\pm4\\sqrt{5}\\maroonD{i}\\end{align}$","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"###Summary \n\n- $\\pm\\sqrt{-80}=\\pm4\\sqrt{5}\\maroonD{i}$","images":{},"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Express the radical using the imaginary unit, $i$.**  \n*Express your answer in simplified form.*\n\n$\\pm\\sqrt{-80}=\\pm$  [[☃ expression 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":true,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"4\\sqrt{5}i"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
